# The fleet's minimum supported version — the forced-update floor.
#
# Leave this file with no value line (comments only) for normal releases.
# When a release ships a BREAKING change that older clients must not keep
# running against (feed schema breaks, protocol breaks, data-format
# migrations without back-compat), put ONE bare release version on its own
# line, e.g.:
#
#   0.6.0
#
# Every CLI feed manifest published from a commit carrying that value embeds
# it as the signed `min_version` field. Running gateways below the floor mark
# the update REQUIRED: the dashboard's update prompt loses its snooze/skip
# affordances until the install is updated. The floor must be a bare release
# (no rc/dev/channel suffix) and must not exceed the version being published
# — `packaging/signing/cli-manifest.py` rejects both at publish time.
#
# Rules:
# - Bump it to the FIRST version that old clients can safely land on, which
#   is usually the breaking release itself.
# - Never bump it in the same release that introduces min_version support
#   itself: clients only learn to read the field after updating once.
# - Lower it (or clear it) only to roll back a mistaken floor; clients above
#   the floor are never affected.
